course: dictionary
lesson: 7270
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and pilot is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the sentence around the word. The context tells you which meaning the writer means.
explain: «Pilots learn real skills in simulators.» Here a pilot is a person who flies a plane or helicopter. Simulators are machines that copy flying, so the clue is the skills, which means the pilot is the flyer.
explain: Pilot can also be a verb. «To pilot» means to fly or steer something. Words like pilot, a noun in one sentence and a verb in another, change their job, but the spelling stays the same. Check the words around it to see which job it does.
fact: A pilot can be a person who flies a plane or helicopter.
fact: A pilot can also be a person who guides big ships into a harbour.
fact: As a verb, «to pilot» means to fly or steer something.
fact: A pilot test or pilot project is a small first try to see if something works.
fact: Carrots help your eyes only if you lack vitamin A; they do not give night vision.
exercise: «Pilots learn real skills in simulators.» What is a pilot in this sentence? | *A person who flies a plane or helicopter | A machine that finds enemy planes | A small first try to see if something works | A kind of vegetable
exercise: A big ship needs help to reach the harbour, so a pilot comes on board to guide it in. What does pilot mean here? | *A person who guides big ships into a harbour | To fly or steer something | A person who flies a plane | A test to see if something works
exercise: What does «to pilot» mean? | To look after passengers | *To fly or steer something | To hide something from enemies | To cook a meal slowly
test: In the Second World War, what was the carrot story partly used to hide? | A new kind of plane | A hidden harbour | Night-time flying lessons | *Radar, a way of finding enemy planes with radio waves
test: What does «a pilot scheme» mean? | *A small first try to see if something works | A time zone used by ships | A carrot used in a war | A plane that flies itself
exam: Which sentence uses pilot as a verb? | The pilot flew the plane across the sea | *She will pilot the small boat into the harbour | Pilots use simulators to practise | The pilot scheme worked well
